**Definition 3.2 (literal sole storage).** Reuse SSA Definitions 3.2 and
4.1–4.2's $F_m$, five-occurrence switches $g_0,g_1$, eight-track cell
$G(c)$, right-spine tape $\mathcal L(w)$ and origin/head links. Replace
only the fixed fully occupied finite-register component by

$$
R(z)=F_q[a(z_1),\ldots,a(z_q)],\qquad
a(\bot)=\bullet,\quad a(0)=g_0,\quad a(1)=g_1,
\tag{CSA.2}
$$

where $z_i=\bot$ means that actual finite location has not been constructed.
Substitute the 64 tape components and $R(z)$ into the outer $F_{65}$.
Call the resulting full ordered tree $U_+(Y)$ and add exactly SSA's
marked-head links to obtain $\Gamma_+(Y)$. The tape-origin links are
absent before the corresponding heads exist and number 65 after acquisition.
There is no descriptor-to-block shortcut.

The structural machine stores these incidences. $Y$ is the comparison
record, not a byte payload maintained beside them. $F_q$ is charged empty
capacity where a bit is absent; it contains no future code value. All
64 tape words are literal, including raw invalid packets and unfinished
copies. Old control versions, banks and dead material remain in place.
Each component has the authority of its actual field. The trusted core's
bounded internal probes grant no owner an all-owner traversal capability.

